  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy, far outperforming image-only ResNet50 (config_010, 20.8%), establishing RNA as the dominant modality. However, we only have one RNA data point and no information on whether multiprofile aggregation adds value. Question: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) directly extends config_001 by changing only the profile setting from single to multi and adding avgpool aggregation, isolating the effect of multi-profile aggregation while keeping the encoder fixed. Why this is best: With only 2 experiments completed, the highest-value uncertainty to reduce is whether the structural choice of multiprofile vs. singleprofile matters for our strongest modality. This is a minimal, confound-free extension of our best result. If multiprofile helps, it validates investing in the broader multiprofile space (including multimodal); if not, it saves budget by narrowing the search. Testing a new encoder (scVI/scGPT) or jumping to multimodal fusion would introduce multiple simultaneous changes and make attribution harder at this early stage."
}

